BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:script-pipeline-first-look-project-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261023T232008Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260930
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261001
SUMMARY:Deadline: Script Pipeline: First Look Project 2026 (screenplay and 
 TV pilot contest)
DESCRIPTION:The 15th annual First Look Project from Script Pipeline searche
 s for higher-concept material across six categories: feature screenplays i
 n Action and Sci-Fi\, Comedy\, Drama\, and Horror and Thriller\, plus hour
  and half-hour original TV pilots. Unlike Script Pipeline's Screenwriting 
 and TV Writing contests\, entries are judged on both writing ability and m
 arket potential\, in addition to originality of concept\; a script that st
 ill needs refining can win if the story could stand out in the current lan
 dscape\, as the aim is a first look at the next buzzworthy specs before th
 ey hit the market. GUIDELINES: screenplays must be feature length\; genres
  without a listed category go to the closest one (Fantasy\, Western or Adv
 enture under Action and Sci-Fi\; Crime and Mystery under Thriller). TV pil
 ots run roughly 30 to 60 pages\, all genres accepted including animation a
 nd genre hybrids. The script must not be under an option or shopping agree
 ment at the time of entry\, and the same script cannot compete in multiple
  categories. CIRCULATION: Script Pipeline's industry relationships (Bellev
 ue Productions\, LBI Entertainment\, Hungry Man\, Alibi Management and oth
 ers) have led to writers signed\, specs sold and films produced. Regular d
 eadline 30 September 2026\; late deadline 15 October\; extended deadline 3
 0 October. Winners announced 15 December 2026.\n\nOrganisation: Script Pip
 eline\nLocation: Online submission\; open to writers worldwide. Script Pip
 eline is based in Los Angeles\, US.\nAward: USD 15\,000 in total prizes ac
 ross six winners: USD 2\,500 to the winner of each of four screenplay genr
 e categories (Action and Sci-Fi\, Comedy\, Drama\, Horror and Thriller) an
 d USD 2\,500 to the winner of each of two TV pilot categories (hour and ha
 lf-hour). All winners also receive long-term circulation to Script Pipelin
 e's industry network of producers\, managers\, agents and directors\, 1-on
 -1 development assistance from Script Pipeline execs\, additional script r
 eviews and consideration of other material\, career guidance and mentorshi
 p\, and invitations to private Symposium events. Entry fee: USD 60 at the 
 regular deadline\, rising to USD 65 (late\, 15 October) and USD 70 (extend
 ed\, 30 October).\nDuration: Winners announced 15 December 2026.\n\nMore: 
 https://scriptpipeline.com/contest/first-look-project?utm_source=artificia
 lnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://scriptpipeline.com/contest/first-look-project?utm_source=artifi
 cialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Online submission\; open to writers worldwide. Script Pipeline is 
 based in Los Angeles\, US.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:amr-paper-of-the-future-prize-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261023T232008Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260901
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260902
SUMMARY:Deadline: AMR: 2026 Paper of the Future Prize
DESCRIPTION:USD 10\,000 prize from the Association for Mathematical Researc
 h for serious experimentation in how mathematicians communicate with one a
 nother\, beyond the static PDF. Submissions should demonstrate communicati
 ve capabilities fundamentally unavailable in a linear paper: interactive e
 xploration of parameter spaces in differential equations\, dynamic visuali
 sation of group actions or geometric structures\, multi-perspective repres
 entations of algebraic or number-theoretic objects\, nonlinear navigation 
 of proof architectures or dependency graphs\, embedded computation as part
  of exposition\, or similar. ELIGIBILITY: no nationality\, institutional o
 r career restriction stated\; the focus is mathematical depth and communic
 ative innovation. This is NOT for popularisation\, production polish or sh
 ort-form video content - it is about novel research-to-research communicat
 ion. EVALUATION CRITERIA: mathematical depth and rigor\; conceptual insigh
 t enabled by the medium\; communicative innovation beyond static expositio
 n\; scalability and reproducibility\; transformative potential for researc
 h communication. PROCESS: initial submissions are a short public YouTube c
 oncept demonstration (with the hashtag #AMRPotF and a concise written expl
 anation of the mathematical substance and communicative innovation in the 
 video description)\, with the YouTube link emailed to PotFPrize@amathr.org
 . Finalists are asked to provide a fully accessible prototype suitable for
  hosting or linking within AMR Reviews\; the winning submission will be pu
 blished in AMR Reviews as an interactive exposition. Selection committee: 
 Mohammed Abouzaid\, Benson Farb\, Alex Kontorovich\, Akshay Venkatesh\, Ma
 ryna Viazovska.\n\nOrganisation: Association for Mathematical Research (AM
 R)\nLocation: Worldwide (digital submission)\nAward: USD 10\,000 prize to 
 the winner\; runner-up recognitions at committee discretion. The committee
  reserves the right to withhold the prize if no submissions meet the stand
 ards.\nDuration: Project-based\n\nMore: https://amathr.org/prizes/paper-of
 -the-future-prize-prize/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=
 referral
URL:https://amathr.org/prizes/paper-of-the-future-prize-prize/?utm_source=a
 rtificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Worldwide (digital submission)
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:next-art-ai-award-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261023T232008Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260930
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261001
SUMMARY:Deadline: AI ART AWARD: NEXT ART AI 2026
DESCRIPTION:NEXT ART AI is an open AI art competition run by the HOBAN Cult
 ural Foundation\, welcoming participants of all backgrounds regardless of 
 career\, nationality or age\, and framed as a way to reflect on the future
  of AI art through new modes of expression and artistic experimentation. T
 WO CATEGORIES: AI IMAGE ART\, for works in a single-image format at 150dpi
  or higher\, submitted as JPG\, JPEG\, PNG or BMP up to 10MB\; and AI VIDE
 O ART\, open to a wide range of video formats including animation\, motion
  graphics and live-action footage enhanced or transformed using AI\, at 10
 80p or higher\, under one minute\, 30 or 60fps recommended\, stereo 48kHz 
 audio recommended\, as mp4 (h.264) or mov. Video entries are submitted as 
 a URL via YouTube\, Vimeo\, Dropbox or OneDrive\, or an alternative platfo
 rm if those are restricted in your region\; links that are inaccessible du
 e to privacy settings may be excluded from judging. WHO CAN ENTER: individ
 uals or teams of up to three including the representative\, though you may
  not submit both as an individual and as part of a team. Team representati
 ves create the account in their own name and all members submit a consent 
 form for personal data. Applicants under 19 need a guardian's signed conse
 nt. One work may be submitted per category. RULES ON AI AND ASSETS: work m
 ust be original and created by the applicant or team\, and must be image o
 r video art created using generative AI platforms. Works that have previou
 sly won an award in another competition are not eligible. Free or paid ext
 ernal assets\, game engines\, AI frameworks\, open-source tools and editin
 g software may be used freely\, but applicants must hold licences permitti
 ng commercial use for every element\, and work infringing third-party righ
 ts is excluded. Even where external assets and editing software are used\,
  the creative process must involve AI\, whether AI-assisted direction\, tr
 ansformation\, generation or other AI-based processes\, and the choice of 
 AI tools\, the scope and method of their use\, and the prompts themselves 
 are all weighed in evaluating the creative use of AI. TIMELINE: applicatio
 ns open 1 September 2026 and close 30 September 2026 at 11:59pm KST\, prel
 iminary round early October\, final round late October\, announcement and 
 ceremony early November\, exhibition late November 2026. Organised and hos
 ted by the HOBAN Cultural Foundation\, sponsored by HOBAN Group\, with Seo
 ul Shinmun and EBN as media partners. Details and schedule are subject to 
 change at the organiser's discretion.\n\nOrganisation: HOBAN Cultural Foun
 dation\nLocation: Online submission\, with the awards ceremony and exhibit
 ion in South Korea. Open to all regardless of career\, nationality or age.
 \nAward: Total prize pool of KRW 21\,000\,000 across 20 winners\, paid aft
 er deduction of applicable taxes and public charges. Grand Prize KRW 5\,00
 0\,000 (selected regardless of category)\; in each of the two categories\,
  First Prize KRW 2\,000\,000\, three Second Prizes of KRW 1\,000\,000 each
 \, and five Honorable Finalist awards of KRW 500\,000 each\; plus a HOBAN 
 Group President's Award of KRW 1\,000\,000. Winners also receive plaques a
 nd certificates\, online and offline exhibition opportunities\, and a feat
 ure on the official online platform. No entry fee is mentioned.\nDuration:
  One-off competition\; exhibition late November 2026\n\nMore: https://next
 -art-ai.com/en/apply/overview?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_me
 dium=referral
URL:https://next-art-ai.com/en/apply/overview?utm_source=artificialnouveaug
 rantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Online submission\, with the awards ceremony and exhibition in Sou
 th Korea. Open to all regardless of career\, nationality or age.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai-philosophy-competition-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261023T232008Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261031
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261101
SUMMARY:Deadline: AI Philosophy Competition: First Edition
DESCRIPTION:The AI Philosophy Competition\, organised by philosophers Zacha
 ry Goodsell and Elliott Thornley and funded by Forethought Research\, aims
  to gauge the philosophical capabilities of AI in a way transparent to the
  philosophical community. Entrants submit up to three original essays on a
 ny philosophical topic\; essays must be primarily AI-generated\, with some
  human guidance allowed\, and each entry must include a methodology report
  explaining how the essay was produced. Essays are capped at 6\,000 words 
 each and may not be previously published or under review elsewhere\; entra
 nts consent to online publication and may choose anonymity. Judging is bli
 nd to methodology and authorship and evaluates the quality and originality
  of the philosophical content (style is not graded)\; the judging committe
 e includes David Chalmers\, John Hawthorne\, Herman Cappelen\, Cian Dorr a
 nd other academic philosophers. PRIZES: USD 3\,000 / 2\,000 / 1\,000 for t
 he top three essays\, plus a USD 5\,000 creative methodology pool. Finalis
 ts announced early December 2026\, results end of January 2027. DEADLINE: 
 31 October 2026.\n\nOrganisation: Zachary Goodsell and Elliott Thornley\, 
 funded by Forethought Research\nLocation: Online submission via OpenReview
  (preferred) or Google Forms\; open internationally.\nAward: USD 3\,000 fi
 rst prize\, USD 2\,000 second\, USD 1\,000 third\, plus a USD 5\,000 pool 
 for creative methodology distributed at the judges' discretion (USD 11\,00
 0 total). No entry fee.\nDuration: Finalists announced early December 2026
 \; results announced end of January 2027.\n\nMore: https://www.zacharygood
 sell.com/ai-philosophy-competition?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&u
 tm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.zacharygoodsell.com/ai-philosophy-competition?utm_source=ar
 tificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Online submission via OpenReview (preferred) or Google Forms\; ope
 n internationally.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:zindi-bias-bounty-mapping-equity-challenge-2026@artificialnouveau.githu
 b.io
DTSTAMP:20261023T232008Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261031
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261101
SUMMARY:Deadline: Zindi: Bias Bounty Mapping Equity Challenge
DESCRIPTION:A bias bounty from Zindi\, Humane Intelligence\, Radiant Earth\
 , and the Heising-Simons Foundation: measure coverage gaps in Overture Map
 s across US Census tracts by comparing it against Census TIGER/Line Roads\
 , Microsoft US Building Footprints\, USGS National Map critical facilities
 \, and Census County Business Patterns. Submissions are automatically eval
 uated with a Bias Score assessing equity metrics across demographic and cl
 imate-vulnerability strata\, surfacing whose neighbourhoods open map data 
 underserves. PRIZES: 1st USD 4\,500\, 2nd USD 2\,500\, 3rd USD 1\,500\, Be
 st Bias Discovery USD 1\,000\, Best Documentation USD 500 (USD 10\,000 tot
 al)\, plus 10\,000 Zindi points. ELIGIBILITY: open to all\, teams of up to
  4. HOW TO ENTER: create a Zindi account\, download the sample submission 
 files\, compute coverage-gap scores per tract GEOID\, and upload a CSV\; 1
 0 submissions per day\, 300 total. Free to enter. DEADLINE: 31 October 202
 6.\n\nOrganisation: Zindi with Humane Intelligence\, Radiant Earth\, and t
 he Heising-Simons Foundation\nLocation: Online\, open to all worldwide\; t
 eams of up to 4.\nAward: USD 10\,000 total in prizes: 1st USD 4\,500\, 2nd
  USD 2\,500\, 3rd USD 1\,500\, Best Bias Discovery USD 1\,000\, Best Docum
 entation USD 500\, plus 10\,000 Zindi points. Free to enter.\nDuration: Ru
 ns 28 August to 31 October 2026\; up to 10 submissions per day\, 300 total
 .\n\nMore: https://zindi.world/competitions/bias-bounty-mapping-equity-cha
 llenge?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://zindi.world/competitions/bias-bounty-mapping-equity-challenge?u
 tm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Online\, open to all worldwide\; teams of up to 4.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:arc-prize-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261023T232008Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261102
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261103
SUMMARY:Deadline: ARC Prize 2026
DESCRIPTION:The ARC Prize Foundation runs its 2026 competition for progress
  toward artificial general intelligence\, with a USD 2\,000\,000 total pri
 ze pool across three tracks: the main Kaggle competition on the ARC-AGI-2 
 static reasoning benchmark\, a track on ARC-AGI-3 interactive agent reason
 ing (second milestone 30 September 2026)\, and a paper prize for research 
 that advances understanding of ARC-AGI performance. Milestone prizes run U
 SD 25\,000 / 10\,000 / 2\,500. Open to individuals and teams worldwide\, e
 ntirely online via Kaggle. Winning entries must be open-sourced under perm
 issive licenses to collect prizes. Main submission deadline 2 November 202
 6\, paper track 8 November 2026\; results announced 4 December 2026.\n\nOr
 ganisation: ARC Prize Foundation\nLocation: Online (Kaggle)\, worldwide\nA
 ward: USD 2\,000\,000 total prize pool across three tracks (ARC-AGI-2\, AR
 C-AGI-3 agents\, and a paper prize)\; milestone prizes include USD 25\,000
  / 10\,000 / 2\,500\nDuration: Competition runs through 2 November 2026 (p
 aper track 8 November)\; results announced 4 December 2026\n\nMore: https:
 //arcprize.org/competitions/2026?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm
 _medium=referral
URL:https://arcprize.org/competitions/2026?utm_source=artificialnouveaugran
 tdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Online (Kaggle)\, worldwide
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:mozilla-data-collective-lost-in-transcription-2026@artificialnouveau.gi
 thub.io
DTSTAMP:20261023T232008Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261002
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261003
SUMMARY:Deadline: Mozilla Data Collective: Lost in Transcription ASR Challe
 nge
DESCRIPTION:Lost in Transcription: Advancing Speech Recognition for Underse
 rved Linguistic Contexts is a machine learning competition on the Mozilla 
 Data Collective platform (run with DrivenData\, backed by Mozilla Foundati
 on). Participants build automatic speech recognition (ASR) models for real
 -world bilingual\, code-switched conversations across three independent tr
 acks: Nahuatl x Spanish\, Indonesian x Javanese\, and North American Spani
 sh x English (Spanglish)\; developers can also work with other languages i
 f the datasets are available on or uploaded to the MDC platform\, which of
 fers ethically sourced multilingual\, multicultural and multimodal dataset
 s. PRIZES: USD 20\,000 total\; per track USD 4\,000 for first place and US
 D 2\,000 for second\, judged by word error rate on a private leaderboard\,
  plus a bonus award for the lowest average word error rate across all thre
 e tracks (same team members required). WHO IS ELIGIBLE: individuals and te
 ams worldwide (students\, tech clubs\, universities\, startup builders\, l
 abs\, independent tinkerers)\; 18+ and legal resident of an eligible juris
 diction\; one account per person\; participants are responsible for comply
 ing with school or employer policies. DEADLINE: the platform lists final s
 ubmissions closing 2 October 2026\, midnight UTC (some announcements said 
 25 September\, so check the platform for your track). Free to enter.\n\nOr
 ganisation: Mozilla Data Collective (Mozilla Foundation)\nLocation: Online
 \, worldwide. Participants must be 18+ (and of age of majority in their ju
 risdiction) and legal residents of an eligible territory\; residents of so
 me territories are excluded from prizes.\nAward: USD 20\,000 total in priz
 es across three language tracks (per track: USD 4\,000 for first place and
  USD 2\,000 for second\, plus a bonus award for the lowest average word er
 ror rate across all three tracks). No entry fee.\nDuration: Winners determ
 ined by word error rate on a private leaderboard after the 2 October 2026 
 close\n\nMore: https://competitions.mozilladatacollective.com/competitions
 /1/lost-in-transcription/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium
 =referral
URL:https://competitions.mozilladatacollective.com/competitions/1/lost-in-t
 ranscription/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Online\, worldwide. Participants must be 18+ (and of age of majori
 ty in their jurisdiction) and legal residents of an eligible territory\; r
 esidents of some territories are excluded from prizes.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:emaf-2027-call-for-entries@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261023T232008Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261215
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261216
SUMMARY:Deadline: EMAF 2027: Call for Entries\, Film / Installation / Expan
 ded
DESCRIPTION:The European Media Art Festival (EMAF) in Osnabrueck invites su
 bmissions for its 2027 edition in three sections: Film (experimental films
  of all lengths and any theme)\, Installation (installative\, interactive\
 , spatial or sculptural media art works) and Expanded (performances\, live
  events or workshops). WHAT YOU GET: all films selected for the Internatio
 nal Selection are equal winners of the EMAF Award with EUR 400 prize money
  each\; films in the Features section (over 60 minutes) receive a EUR 250 
 screening fee\; curated programmes pay EUR 80-250 depending on length\; in
 stallations and expanded projects receive a EUR 500 fee with production co
 sts paid by the festival. Selected artists are invited to the festival wit
 h free accreditation\, three hotel nights (potentially longer if setting u
 p is required) and a contribution to travel costs. RULES: maximum 2 works 
 per artist\; only works completed in 2026 or 2027 are eligible\; no premie
 re status required\; works entered at previous editions will not be recons
 idered. Films up to 60 minutes are viewed for the International Selection\
 , films over 60 minutes for Features. Installation entries should relate t
 o the 2027 festival theme of the archive (as an instrument of knowledge pr
 oduction\, a site of critical intervention and a space for alternative vis
 ions of the future)\; Installation and Expanded entries must include a com
 prehensive description\, tech rider\, cost calculation and visual material
 s. Non-English-language works must have English subtitles for the selectio
 n screening. Submit digitally via the EMAF registration portal (no DVDs or
  physical media). Selection decisions are emailed from mid-March 2027. DEA
 DLINE: the call closes as soon as 2\,200 entries have been received\, or a
 t the latest on 15 December 2026\, so submit early. No entry fee.\n\nOrgan
 isation: European Media Art Festival (EMAF)\nLocation: Osnabrueck\, German
 y. Open worldwide\; selected artists are invited to the festival with free
  accreditation\, three hotel nights and a contribution to travel costs.\nA
 ward: All films in the International Selection are equal winners of the EM
 AF Award and receive EUR 400 each. Screening fees: EUR 250 for Features\, 
 EUR 80-250 for curated programmes depending on length\, EUR 500 for instal
 lations and expanded projects\; production costs for installations and exp
 anded projects are paid by the festival. Selected artists get free accredi
 tation\, three hotel nights (longer if setup requires) and a travel cost c
 ontribution. No entry fee.\nDuration: Festival in Osnabrueck\, spring 2027
 \; screening prints must arrive by 1 April 2027\n\nMore: https://emaf.film
 chief.com/entry-forms?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=ref
 erral
URL:https://emaf.filmchief.com/entry-forms?utm_source=artificialnouveaugran
 tdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Osnabrueck\, Germany. Open worldwide\; selected artists are invite
 d to the festival with free accreditation\, three hotel nights and a contr
 ibution to travel costs.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:hm-foundation-global-change-award-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261023T232008Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261002
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261003
SUMMARY:Deadline: H&M Foundation: Global Change Award 2027 (via The Mills F
 abrica nomination window)
DESCRIPTION:The H&M Foundation backs ten changemakers each year with a EUR 
 200\,000 grant to accelerate early-stage innovation toward a net-zero text
 ile industry\; since 2015 the award has distributed a combined EUR 10 mill
 ion to 56 innovations. The foundation's FAQ states applicants can be an in
 dividual\, a small team or an organisation\, with no registered-company re
 quirement\, and ideas can still be at research\, lab or concept stage. Nei
 ther the Foundation\, its partners nor H&M Group take any equity or IP rig
 hts\, so this is a genuine grant\, not an investment vehicle. CATEGORIES: 
 sustainable materials\, responsible production\, mindful consumption\, and
  wildcards. WHAT YOU GET: EUR 200\,000 plus a yearlong Changemaker Program
 me with industry knowledge\, tools and connections. HOW TO APPLY: the 2027
  cycle is nomination-based\; The Mills Fabrica is an official nominator ac
 cepting open proposals from 1 September to 2 October 2026 via its website.
  DEADLINE: 2 October 2026 for the Mills Fabrica proposal window.\n\nOrgani
 sation: H&M Foundation (proposals via official nominator The Mills Fabrica
 )\nLocation: Worldwide. Open to early-stage textile and fashion innovators
 \; individuals\, small teams and organisations\, no registered-company req
 uirement.\nAward: EUR 200\,000 grant per winner\, ten winners annually\, p
 lus a yearlong Changemaker Programme. No equity or IP is taken. Participat
 ion is free of charge.\nDuration: Yearlong Changemaker Programme accompani
 es the grant.\n\nMore: https://hmfoundation.com/gca/?utm_source=artificial
 nouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://hmfoundation.com/gca/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm
 _medium=referral
LOCATION:Worldwide. Open to early-stage textile and fashion innovators\; in
 dividuals\, small teams and organisations\, no registered-company requirem
 ent.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:loewe-foundation-craft-prize-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261023T232008Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261015
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261016
SUMMARY:Deadline: LOEWE FOUNDATION: Craft Prize 2027
DESCRIPTION:The 10th edition of the LOEWE FOUNDATION Craft Prize is open fo
 r registration until 15 October 2026. Established in 2016\, the prize rewa
 rds works combining technical excellence\, artistic quality and innovation
  in craft. WHAT YOU GET: the winner receives EUR 50\,000\, and shortlisted
  works are shown in an exhibition in Europe in spring 2027. DISCIPLINES: t
 extiles are explicitly listed among the eligible craft disciplines\, along
 side ceramics\, woodwork\, metalwork and other applied arts\, which makes 
 the prize a home for e-textile and material-innovation work with a craft d
 imension. ELIGIBILITY: entries must be original one-of-a-kind works made e
 ntirely or partly by hand\, created within the last five years\, and not p
 reviously awarded a prize\; applicants must be professionals at least 18 y
 ears old\, and individuals and collectives of all nationalities may apply.
  DEADLINE: registration closes 15 October 2026 at 23:59 CET.\n\nOrganisati
 on: LOEWE FOUNDATION\nLocation: Worldwide\; shortlist exhibition in Europe
  in spring 2027. Open to professional artisans aged 18 or over\, individua
 ls or collectives\, all nationalities.\nAward: EUR 50\,000 for the winning
  entry. No application fee.\nDuration: One-off prize\; shortlisted works s
 hown in an exhibition in Europe in spring 2027.\n\nMore: https://craftpriz
 e.loewe.com/en/craftprize2027?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_me
 dium=referral
URL:https://craftprize.loewe.com/en/craftprize2027?utm_source=artificialnou
 veaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Worldwide\; shortlist exhibition in Europe in spring 2027. Open to
  professional artisans aged 18 or over\, individuals or collectives\, all 
 nationalities.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:oberhausen-73-call-for-films-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261023T232008Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270118
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270119
SUMMARY:Deadline: Internationale Kurzfilmtage Oberhausen: Call for Films\, 
 73rd Festival (2027)
DESCRIPTION:The 73rd International Short Film Festival Oberhausen (27 April
  to 2 May 2027)\, one of the oldest and most influential short film festiv
 als\, opens its call for films across five competitions: International (ma
 x 35 minutes\, produced outside Germany\, German festival premiere require
 d)\, German (max 45 minutes\, produced in Germany\, no premiere requiremen
 t)\, NRW (max 45 minutes\, produced or co-produced in North Rhine-Westphal
 ia)\, International Children's and Youth Film\, and the MuVi Award for mus
 ic videos produced in Germany (max 15 minutes). ELIGIBILITY: works produce
 d after 1 January 2026\; screening formats 35mm\, 16mm\, Super 8 and DCP (
 MuVi: DCP). PRIZES: from the EUR 8\,000 Grand Prize of the City of Oberhau
 sen and EUR 4\,000 Principal Prize through German\, NRW\, children's/youth
 \, FIPRESCI\, Ecumenical and audience prizes\, awarded to the directors\, 
 plus European Film Awards and ECFA nominations. FEES: the first five submi
 ssions per submitter are free of charge\; from the sixth\, a EUR 20 handli
 ng fee per film applies. HOW TO SUBMIT: online entry form with preview lin
 k via kurzfilmtage.filmchief.com\; selection results announced mid-March 2
 027. DEADLINE: 18 January 2027 for all competitions (17:00 UTC per the lis
 ting)\, except the MuVi Award: 22 February 2027. No extensions.\n\nOrganis
 ation: Internationale Kurzfilmtage Oberhausen (International Short Film Fe
 stival Oberhausen)\nLocation: Oberhausen\, Germany. International Competit
 ion open to productions from outside Germany (plus co-productions)\; separ
 ate German\, NRW\, Children's and Youth\, and MuVi competitions.\nAward: I
 nternational Competition: Grand Prize of the City of Oberhausen EUR 8\,000
 \, Principal Prize EUR 4\,000\, Promotional Prize EUR 1\,500\, plus a Euro
 pean Film Awards short film nomination. German Competition: EUR 5\,000 mai
 n prize\, EUR 1\,500 promotional\, EUR 2\,500 3sat Emerging Talent Prize (
 with purchase offer)\, EUR 1\,000 ZONTA Prize for a female filmmaker. NRW 
 Competition: EUR 1\,000 and EUR 500 prizes\, plus NRW Ministry prizes of E
 UR 5\,000 and EUR 3\,000\, FIPRESCI Prize\, EUR 2\,000 Ecumenical Jury Pri
 ze\, EUR 750 WDR Westart Audience Jury Prize. Children's and Youth: severa
 l EUR 1\,000-1\,500 prizes and an ECFA Short Film Award nomination. Prizes
  go to the directors. SUBMISSION FEE: first five submissions per submitter
  are free\; EUR 20 handling fee per film from the sixth.\nDuration: Festiv
 al runs 27 April to 2 May 2027.\n\nMore: https://www.kurzfilmtage.de/en/fe
 stival/submission/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referr
 al
URL:https://www.kurzfilmtage.de/en/festival/submission/?utm_source=artifici
 alnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Oberhausen\, Germany. International Competition open to production
 s from outside Germany (plus co-productions)\; separate German\, NRW\, Chi
 ldren's and Youth\, and MuVi competitions.
END:VEVENT
