UID:jmem-new-media-award-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261023T232008Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261108
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261109
SUMMARY:Deadline: Judson-Morrissey Excellence in New Media Award 2026 (BIPO
 C students)
DESCRIPTION:The Judson-Morrissey Excellence in New Media Award (JMEM) is th
 e New Media Caucus's scholarship program supporting BIPOC students in new 
 media art fields. It gives multiple unrestricted monetary awards of up to 
 USD 500 each\, funded through donor contributions\, and features awardees 
 in an NMC Header/Footer Gallery exhibition and a digitally published inter
 view. ELIGIBILITY: BIPOC undergraduate and graduate students working as ar
 tists\, practitioners\, historians and/or critics in new media art. TO APP
 LY: submit the Google Form with an application letter (max 500 words)\, a 
 100-200 word biography\, and either 3-5 artwork samples or 2-3 writing sam
 ples. DEADLINE: 8 November 2026\, 11:59 PM EST. Questions to NMC co-presid
 ent Chanhee Choi.\n\nOrganisation: New Media Caucus\nLocation: Online appl
 ication\; the New Media Caucus is an international nonprofit. Open to BIPO
 C undergraduate and graduate students in new media art fields.\nAward: Mul
 tiple unrestricted awards of varying amounts up to USD 500 each\, funded t
 hrough donor contributions. Awardees are also featured in an NMC Header/Fo
 oter Gallery exhibition and a digitally published interview. Free to apply
 .\n\nMore: https://newmediacaucus.org/opportunities/jmem-scholarship-open-
 call?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://newmediacaucus.org/opportunities/jmem-scholarship-open-call?utm
 _source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Online application\; the New Media Caucus is an international nonp
 rofit. Open to BIPOC undergraduate and graduate students in new media art 
 fields.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:arts-convergences-video-prize-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261023T232008Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261019
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261020
SUMMARY:Deadline: Arts Convergences Video Prize\, 6th edition (short films 
 on mental illness)
DESCRIPTION:The Arts Convergences Video Prize rewards very short films that
  raise public awareness of the lives of adults living with mental illness\
 , showing their difficulties but above all their talents and their ability
  to move us. Sixth edition\, run with Thanks for Nothing and supported by 
 the City of Paris\, Psycom\, the Centre Hospitalier de Plaisir and the Fal
 ret Foundation. FORMAT: 90 seconds to 4 minutes\, any genre (comedy\, thri
 ller\, documentary\, news report\, animation\, stills\, motion) and any ca
 mera. IMPORTANT EXCLUSIONS: the rules explicitly disallow artistic videos 
 of an experimental nature\, music videos\, advertisements\, institutional 
 films and prevention campaigns\, so frame the work as a narrative or docum
 entary short rather than video art. Videos in languages other than French 
 are disqualified without French subtitles\, and end credits must include a
  mandatory partnership mention. ELIGIBILITY: open to anyone over 18 who ho
 lds the rights to the video\; candidates produce the film at their own cos
 t. SELECTION: jury of professionals judges relevance to the theme first\, 
 then originality and creativity\, then technical quality\; 15 shortlisted 
 videos go to a public online vote about 3 weeks before the ceremony. Selec
 ted candidates transfer non-commercial worldwide rights for 10 years and t
 he organisers guarantee a public presentation of selected videos in a lead
 ing cultural institution at their cost. Deadline 19 October 2026\, midnigh
 t CET\, via the candidate space on the website. Awards ceremony 26 Novembe
 r 2026 at the Forum des Images\, Paris\, open to the public.\n\nOrganisati
 on: Arts Convergences\, in partnership with Thanks for Nothing\nLocation: 
 Open internationally\; organizer based in France. Submission is online\; w
 inners should attend or be represented at the awards ceremony in Paris (26
  November 2026\, Forum des Images). Videos not in French must carry French
  subtitles.\nAward: EUR 5\,000 total: Grand Prize EUR 2\,000\, Jury Prize 
 EUR 1\,500\, Public Choice Prize EUR 1\,500 (online vote). Additional priz
 es may be awarded. No entry fee.\nDuration: One-off prize for a finished v
 ery short film.\n\nMore: https://artsconvergences.com/prix-video/?utm_sour
 ce=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://artsconvergences.com/prix-video/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugr
 antdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Open internationally\; organizer based in France. Submission is on
 line\; winners should attend or be represented at the awards ceremony in P
 aris (26 November 2026\, Forum des Images). Videos not in French must carr
 y French subtitles.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:fondation-schneider-talents-contemporains-water-2026@artificialnouveau.
 github.io
DTSTAMP:20261023T232008Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261122
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261123
SUMMARY:Deadline: Fondation Francois Schneider: Talents Contemporains 16th 
 Edition - Water
DESCRIPTION:The Fondation Francois Schneider's Talents Contemporains compet
 ition\, in its 16th edition\, supports contemporary creation on the theme 
 of WATER. Submissions can be a project for an installation or sculpture\, 
 or an existing unique work in painting\, drawing\, sculpture\, installatio
 n\, photography\, video\, textile art or other fine and visual arts\; perf
 orming arts and music are excluded. A Grand Jury (chaired by international
  museum figures) designates 4 to 7 laureates. WHAT YOU GET: EUR 15\,000 pe
 r laureate as a merit prize and official acquisition of the artwork (EUR 8
 \,000 for editioned works)\; installation and sculpture projects share up 
 to EUR 50\,000 in production assistance (existing works get no production 
 budget)\; plus an exhibition at the foundation's centre in Wattwiller\, a 
 bilingual publication\, inclusion in the collection and a video portrait. 
 ELIGIBILITY: visual artists of all nationalities\, of legal age\, with a s
 olid professional background and/or an art school degree and a recent cont
 inuous track record over the past five years (exhibitions\, publications o
 r residencies)\; one artwork or project per candidate per year. Applicatio
 ns in French (French speakers) or English (all others)\, via the foundatio
 n's online platform. DEADLINE: 22 November 2026.\n\nOrganisation: Fondatio
 n Francois Schneider\nLocation: Wattwiller\, France. Open internationally 
 to visual artists of all nationalities (legal age).\nAward: EUR 15\,000 pe
 r laureate (merit prize plus acquisition of the work\; EUR 8\,000 when the
  work is part of a multiple edition\, e.g. photo or video)\; up to 7 laure
 ates. Sculpture and installation projects can additionally receive up to E
 UR 50\,000 in production assistance. No entry fee stated.\nDuration: Call 
 open 23 September to 22 November 2026. Laureates get an exhibition at the 
 foundation's art centre in Wattwiller\, a bilingual publication\, entry in
 to the collection and a video portrait.\n\nMore: https://www.fondationfran
 coisschneider.org/en/contemporary-talents-competition/contemporary-talents
 -competition-water-wattwiller/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_m
 edium=referral
URL:https://www.fondationfrancoisschneider.org/en/contemporary-talents-comp
 etition/contemporary-talents-competition-water-wattwiller/?utm_source=arti
 ficialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Wattwiller\, France. Open internationally to visual artists of all
  nationalities (legal age).
END:VEVENT
END:VCALENDAR
